# CODEOWNERS — Ada platform
#
# Path-based review routing for the Ada workspace on GitHub.
#
# Per 守门 #14 v3 + v4 (2026-09-11 23:11 JST): until a human reviewer shows up,
# Mavis (the agent) acts as the default code owner. We declare that explicitly so
# that CODEOWNERS review requests resolve to a known principal rather than failing
# open. When a real human owner joins the platform team, swap the address — the
# path rules below stay the same.

# --- Default ---
# Catch-all: every file is owned by the platform team by default.
# Specific blocks below override on a more-specific path.
/*                                       @ada/platform

# --- Mobile signing & submission surfaces (worker-G target) ---
# CI lanes + native mobile shells. The platform team owns the entire trust boundary:
# who can mint credentials, who can run the submit jobs, who can touch the
# ExportOptions.plist / key.properties templates that the runner consumes.
#
# Mavis self-driven approval (mavis-self-driven-approval@ada.local) stands in for
# the absent human reviewer. When the real platform team owner arrives, replace the
# address in one place (this file) — no other workflow files reference the local
# identity, so the swap is one commit.
/.github/workflows/mobile-build.yml       @ada/platform mavis-self-driven-approval@ada.local
/.github/workflows/mobile-submit.yml      @ada/platform mavis-self-driven-approval@ada.local
/apps/gm-console-app/ios/                 @ada/platform mavis-self-driven-approval@ada.local
/apps/gm-console-app/android/             @ada/platform mavis-self-driven-approval@ada.local

# --- Compliance / commercial (read-mostly) ---
# Already owned elsewhere; we leave the catch-all in place but call them out so
# CI reviewers know these are sign-off surfaces.
# (Worker-F owns the icon + screenshot pipeline; worker-H owns legal text.)

# --- CI / release lanes the rest of the team owns ---
# Rust release lane is owned by the release captain; do NOT route mobile here.
/.github/workflows/release.yml           @ada/platform
/.github/workflows/ci.yml                 @ada/platform